⛵ Lagos Yacht Club
Founded in 1932, sits at Magazine Point on Lagos Island, near the Army Officers’ Mess and across Independence Bridge from Victoria Island. Overlooking Lagos Harbour, it offers a unique vantage point for watching ships and yachts move through the waterways while experiencing Lagos’ long-standing sailing tradition. 

Today, sailing is at the heart of the club. Members can learn to sail, take part in yacht races, and compete in Saturday and public-holiday races, while experienced sailors participate in national championships. The club also organizes special events, including the challenging 140 km overnight Badagry Race.

Beyond racing, the club provides a social setting with its clubhouse and restaurant, while its facilities and sailing activities give members opportunities to enjoy Lagos’ waterways in a very different way. For anyone interested in experiencing sailing firsthand, the club also offers training for people who may have no previous sailing experience. ⛵🌊

